Z||000004||JohnF||12-12-2001||05:59 PM||||Go to the Daytime Running LIghts thread that ran about 4 weeks ago for a lot of opinions and choices.<P>"Fog" lamps are usually used during the day and are amber in color.  DRLs (Daytime Running Lights) are both clear and amber.  Fog lamps are usually controllable with some kind of ON/OFF switch.   DRLs are usually automatic and function with the ignition key.<P>Having said all that, here is my DRLs.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56100346&Sequence=0"> <P>Note, that these use the "bright" element of the Fiero turn signal, just like current 'vettes and Trans Ams, etc.  <P>When headlights are turned on, they revert to normanl Fiero lights automatically.  When turn signal is used, they also revert to normal operation.  Anytime the key is in the "run" position, these light are automatically ON.  <P>No, they are not blinding anytime.  Can they be seen?  Can you see a new 'vette?<P>Less than one hour and less than $30 to install.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||6
Z||000005||JohnF||12-12-2001||05:59 PM||||Go to the Daytime Running LIghts thread that ran about 4 weeks ago for a lot of opinions and choices.<P>"Fog" lamps are usually used during the day and are amber in color.  DRLs (Daytime Running Lights) are both clear and amber.  Fog lamps are usually controllable with some kind of ON/OFF switch.   DRLs are usually automatic and function with the ignition key.<P>Having said all that, here is my DRLs.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56100346&Sequence=0"> <P>Note, that these use the "bright" element of the Fiero turn signal, just like current 'vettes and Trans Ams, etc.  <P>When headlights are turned on, they revert to normanl Fiero lights automatically.  When turn signal is used, they also revert to normal operation.  Anytime the key is in the "run" position, these light are automatically ON.  <P>No, they are not blinding anytime.  Can they be seen?  Can you see a new 'vette?<P>Less than one hour and less than $30 to install.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||6
